{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdqfGh6xTUC3Qx1NxZizR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Plan\n\n1. **Add `check:pricing-sync` to pre-commit hook as a blocking check.**\n   Wire it into `.husky/pre-commit` (or equivalent) so it runs and blocks commits locally before code reaches CI. This catches drift immediately and shifts the pain earlier in the developer workflow.\n\n2. **Do NOT delete the `pricing-sync` job from CI; instead, make it non-blocking.**\n   Keep the CI job running (it's cheap at ~2 seconds) but remove its required status, because pre-commit hooks can be bypassed (`git commit --no-verify`) and CI is the ultimate enforcement gate. A non-blocking job serves as a safety net and audit trail without blocking merges."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":300,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":161,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
